#: infopage.cpp:37
msgid ""
"_: Translators, feel free to add yourself in the text below, asking for a "
"postcard ;-), also feel free to add a section saying "
"<h2>Translators</h2>. Kind regards, and thanks for your work - Jesper.\n"
"<h1>Regular Expression Editor</h1>"
"<p>What you are currently looking at is an editor for <i>Regular "
"Expressions</i>.</p>"
"<p>The upper part in the middle is the editing area, the lower part is a "
"verification window where you can try your regular expressions right away. "
"The row of buttons is the editing actions. This is actually very similar to "
"common drawing programs. Select an editing tool to start editing your "
"regular expression, and press the mouse button in the editing area where you "
"want this item inserted.</p>"
"<p>For a more detailed description of this editor see the <a "
"href=\"doc://\">info pages</a></p>"
"<h2>What is a regular expression?</h2>If you do not know what a regular "
"expression is, then it might be a good idea to read <a "
"href=\"doc://whatIsARegExp\">the introduction to regular expressions</a>.<p>"
msgstr ""

#: infopage.cpp:55
msgid ""
"<h2>Send the author an electronic postcard</h2>I don't get any money for "
"working on KRegExpEditor, I therefore appreciate it very much when users "
"tell me what they think about my work. I would therefore be very happy if "
"you <a href=\"mailto:blackie@kde.org?subject=KRegExpEditor\">"
"sent me a short mail</a>, telling me that you use my regular expression "
"editor."
"<h2>Author</h2><a href=\"http://www.blackie.dk/\">Jesper K. Pedersen</a> "
"&lt;<a href=\"mailto:blackie@kde.org\">blackie@kde.org</a>&gt;"
msgstr ""

